// examples/hydramodem/melos.exsc -- HydraModem's MUSICAL transmitter, the
// `melody` profile, as pure functions: given a frame's seventeen bytes, the
// note of each of its 124 symbols, and the sample any point of the waveform
// becomes. The sibling of modulator.exsc (the default profile), and pure the
// same way: no `poscit`, no capability-bearing parameter, no `initium`.
// melos_emitte.exsc walks the layout and writes the bytes.
//
// The reference is Punctim's hydramodem/ at 5c6a4e1 -- `hydra_profile_melody`
// (hydra_profile.c) and the exact synthesis `music_render` (hydra_modem.c),
// specified in its docs/MUSIC.md, "Exact synthesis" -- and
// vendor/hydramodem-melos/ holds what its frame_tx rendered, which this
// program reproduces byte for byte (tests/programs/melos_*/).
// docs/design/melos.md is the design.
//
// The profile: 48 kHz, 25 baud (1920 samples a symbol), 8-FSK whose tones are
// the major pentatonic on the harmonic series of the baud -- harmonics 24 27
// 30 36 40 48 54 60 of 25 Hz, 600 to 1500 Hz, just intonation -- Gray-mapped
// onto the symbols; a 12-symbol preamble, sync word 0x2DD4, CRC-16, the K=7
// rate-1/2 code, interleaved, all as modulator.exsc has them; a drone on
// harmonics 12 and 18 (300 and 450 Hz) at 0.12 each; a 10 ms raised-cosine
// attack and release outside the symbol body.
//
// Every tone and drone completes a whole number of cycles in 1920 samples, so
// every phase this transmitter needs is k/1920 of a cycle for an integer k:
// the waveform is one sine table and a fixed order of binary64 operations,
// the reference's own, repeated here. As in modulator.exsc there is no
// bitwise and or or, no integer division or remainder and no signed integer:
// a remainder is a walk, a negative sample is `0 -% v` in u16. Floating
// point is used where the reference uses it, and only there.

// ---- the layout ------------------------------------------------------------

// hydra_modem.c, hydra_modem_tx: lead = 0.02 x 48000 + R silence each side,
// with the span -- R samples of pre-roll, the symbols, R of post-roll --
// starting R before the body. So 960 zeros, 480 + 124 x 1920 + 480 = 239,040
// samples of span, 960 zeros: 240,960 samples, 481,920 bytes of audio after
// a 44-byte header.
publica firma melos_silentium: mensura = 960;
publica firma melos_rampa: mensura = 480;             // R: 10 ms
publica firma melos_symbola: mensura = 124;           // 12 + 6 + 106
publica firma melos_exempla_symboli: mensura = 1920;  // L = 48000 / 25

publica functio melos_caput() -> Caput {
    redde Caput {
        riff: 0x52494646,
        magnitudo: 481956,
        wave: 0x57415645,
        fmt: 0x666d7420,
        fmt_longitudo: 16,
        codex: 1,
        canales: 1,
        frequentia: 48000,
        octeti_secundo: 96000,
        passus: 2,
        latitudo: 16,
        data: 0x64617461,
        longitudo: 481920
    };
}

// ---- the sine ----------------------------------------------------------------

// Q[k] = sin(2 pi k / 1920) for 0 <= k <= 480, the first quarter wave: the
// reference's qsin computes exactly these with libm, as
// sin((2.0 * M_PI * k) / 1920.0) (0.0 at k = 0), and folds every other k by
// symmetry, so the whole table is these 481 binary64 values
// (vendor/hydramodem-melos/PROVENANCE.md, "The quarter-wave table").
//
// They are written as M[k] = Q[k] x 2^61, integers, not as decimals. A float
// literal carries at most fifteen significant digits (spec §8.4, EXS-E0308),
// and fifteen do not pin a binary64 -- seventeen do. Every Q[k] is an integer
// multiple of 2^-61 (the smallest nonzero entry, Q[1] = 0.00327..., is above
// 2^-9, so its last mantissa bit is worth 2^-61 or more), so M[k] is exact,
// M[k] < 2^61 + 1, and each has at most 53 significant bits: `sicut f64`
// converts it without rounding, and dividing by 2^61, a power of two,
// rounds nothing either. So `melos_quadrans` rebuilds the reference's 481
// values bit for bit. What the CERTIFICATE pins is less: the WAV's bytes, and
// a 16-bit sample does not see the last bits of a binary64 -- one entry moved
// by 2 ulp still certifies (docs/design/melos.md, the negative controls). The
// table's exactness rests on the arithmetic above, not on the test.
//
// Functions returning the literals, not module `firma`s, for the reason
// modulator.exsc's tabula_sinus gives. The writer binds the table once per
// WAV and passes it down.
